    "status": "completed",
    "summary": "Fixed. `python3 -m pytest -q` passes (1 passed).\n\n**Change** — `memo.py`: rewrote `Memo.get` to be thread-safe:\n- A single `threading.Lock` guards `self.values` and a new `_in_progress` dict mapping key → `threading.Event`.\n- Caller under lock: cached → return value (identity preserved, `None` handled via `key in values` instead of the original `value is None` check, which was the None-caching bug).\n- If another thread is computing that key → release lock and `event.wait()`, then loop and read the cached value (or re-attempt if it failed).\n- Otherwise the caller claims the key: runs the factory **outside** any lock, then publishes the value and sets the event; on any exception (`BaseException`) it removes the in-progress entry and sets the event so waiters wake up and a later attempt can run — nothing is cached.\n- Per-key events + factory running outside the lock means a blocked factory on one key never blocks other keys.\n\n**Verification** — beyond the public test, I ran a scratch harness (since deleted) covering: 8 threads racing one factory (one run, shared result, `None` cached), exception propagating to runner and waiter with the key left unset for retry, a blocked key not stalling another key, 200 randomized flaky-factory rounds, and a 70-thread/7-key stress run — all passed.\n\nNo other files touched; `test_public.py` and `pyproject.toml` untouched.",
